// REQUIRES: host-linux-amd64 || host-linux-arm64
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/run-golden.py --src %S/Inputs/own/delete-range.gopp %S/Inputs/own/delete-range.out
// GOLDEN: by-hand
// P04.09 review R6 (spec 8.3): `delete(m, k)` and `move(m[k])` of the entry a
// range is on take it out of the map at once, but its key and value are
// dropped at the end of that iteration (`v` still reads the old value, as Go
// prints it); removing another entry drops it at once. The map's running
// iterations know the entry each is on (map_delete). The drops print (Go++
// only).
